Friday desktop shell (apps/desktop)

Some Windows techniques in src-tauri/src (island.rs, platform_windows.rs,
shortcuts.rs, lib.rs) were learned from the MIT-licensed source code of the
project "coucou" (https://github.com/Louis-CFM/coucou), and re-implemented here:

  - click-through by a cursor poll: a thread reads the cursor every 16 ms,
    hit-tests the island rectangle the page reports, grown by a 14 px margin,
    and toggles the window's ignore-cursor-events flag on the same tick;
  - a non-activating tool window (WS_EX_NOACTIVATE, WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW) that
    takes the keyboard only when a text field needs it;
  - every webview created at start with identical WebView2 arguments, and
    overlay windows parked off-screen instead of hidden;
  - placement at the top centre of a monitor in physical pixels, set again
    after a move across monitors;
  - the AltGr check: a Ctrl+Alt shortcut that types a character on an
    installed keyboard layout (ToUnicodeEx) is not registered.

No names, characters, artwork, icons, expressions, geometry, colours or sounds
were taken from that project. Its names and its character are reserved by
their author and are not used by Friday. Friday's icons are drawn in code from
Friday's own mark (apps/ui/public/favicon.svg; scripts/make-icons.mjs and
src-tauri/src/tray.rs).

